{"id":"mikro","name":"GPIO, PWM & ADC","untertitel":"GPIO-Pins, PWM, ADC und Takt","farbe":"#a6e22e","symbol":"wechselspannung","reihenfolge":8,"seiten":[{"id":"pwm","titel":"PWM & Timer","kurz":"Tastverhältnis, Frequenz, Auflösung","tags":["pwm","tastverhältnis","duty","timer","dimmen","servo","frequenz","mittelwert","led"],"bloecke":[{"t":"text","text":["**PWM** (Pulsweitenmodulation) schaltet ein Signal schnell ein und aus. Das **Tastverhältnis** (Duty Cycle) bestimmt den Mittelwert: 25 % an → im Mittel 25 % der Spannung."]},{"t":"formel","name":"Mittelwert und Frequenz","f":"U_mittel = U · D        f = 1 / T        D = t_ein / T","text":""},{"t":"rechner","titel":"PWM-Rechner","felder":[["u","Spannung","V","3,3"],["d","Tastverhältnis","%","25"],["f","Frequenz","Hz","1k"]],"ergebnis":[["um","Mittelwert","u*d/100","V"],["t","Periodendauer","1/f","s"],["ton","Einschaltzeit","d/100/f","s"]]},{"t":"rechner","titel":"Timer → PWM-Frequenz (AVR / Arduino)","felder":[["fcpu","CPU-Takt","Hz","16M"],["pre","Vorteiler","","64"],["n","Zählerbreite (Bits)","","8"]],"ergebnis":[["f","PWM-Frequenz (Fast PWM)","fcpu/(pre*2**n)","Hz"]]},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Anwendung","Frequenz","Hinweis"],"zeilen":[["LED-Dimmen","500 Hz – 20 kHz","> 100 Hz flimmerfrei, > 20 kHz unhörbar"],["Servo","50 Hz","1–2 ms"],["DC-Motor","1–20 kHz","unhörbar > 20 kHz"],["Lüfter (4-Pin)","25 kHz","Intel-Spec"],["Netzteil (Buck)","100 kHz – 2 MHz","Schaltfrequenz"],["Audio-DAC (PWM)","> 100 kHz + Filter","Tiefpass nötig"]],"mono":[],"fett":true},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Pi-Hardware-PWM","Pins"],"zeilen":[["PWM0 Kanal 0","GPIO12, GPIO18"],["PWM0 Kanal 1","GPIO13, GPIO19"]],"mono":[],"fett":true,"titel":"Hardware-PWM (stabil), Rest per Software"},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"Mit PWM-Pins dimmt man **LED-Streifen** über einen MOSFET. Auflösung mit 8 Bit = 256 Stufen, 10 Bit = 1024, 12 Bit = 4096."},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"warn","text":"PWM an induktiven Lasten (Motor): Freilaufdiode nicht vergessen und Frequenz oberhalb des Hörbereichs wählen, sonst **pfeift** der Motor."},{"t":"h2","text":"PWM-Mittelwert"},{"t":"text","text":["Tastverhältnis (Duty) und Spitzenspannung → mittlere Spannung."]},{"t":"formel","name":"PWM-Mittelwert","f":"Umittel = U · Duty","text":""},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"PWM schaltet schnell zwischen 0 und U: der Mittelwert ist U · Duty."},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"RC-Tiefpass macht daraus eine glatte Gleichspannung (Grenzfrequenz weit unter der PWM-Frequenz)."},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"Angeschlossene Last nie direkt am Pin betreiben – Servos brauchen eine eigene 5-V-Versorgung (Masse verbinden)."}],"siehe":["halbleiter:mosfet","bt_module:motoren","raspi:gpio"],"symbol":"sinus","gruppe":""},{"id":"adc","titel":"ADC & DAC","kurz":"Auflösung, LSB, Referenz, Abtasttheorem","tags":["adc","dac","auflösung","mcp3008","ads1115","abtast","nyquist","analog","bit","referenz","lsb"],"bloecke":[{"t":"formel","name":"Auflösung (LSB)","f":"LSB = U_ref / 2ⁿ","text":""},{"t":"formel","name":"Messwert","f":"Code = U_in / U_ref · (2ⁿ − 1)","text":""},{"t":"rechner","titel":"ADC-Rechner","felder":[["u","Eingangsspannung","V",""],["ur","Referenz","V","3,3"],["n","Bits","","12"],["c","ADC-Code","","2048"]],"formeln":{"u":["c/(2**n-1)*ur"],"c":["u/ur*(2**n-1)"]},"text":"Lass ein Feld leer – es wird aus den anderen berechnet. Schreibweise: 4k7, 10u, 2,2M, 100n."},{"t":"rechner","titel":"Auflösung","felder":[["ur","Referenz","V","3,3"],["n","Bits","","12"]],"ergebnis":[["lsb","1 LSB","ur/2**n","V"],["s","Stufen","2**n","","ganz"]]},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["ADC","Bits","Kanäle","Schnittstelle","Hinweis"],"zeilen":[["Arduino Uno intern","10","6","–","0–5 V"],["ESP32 intern","12","18","–","nicht linear!"],["Pico intern","12","3 + Temp","–","ENOB ≈ 9"],["MCP3008","10","8","SPI","Pi-Standard, günstig"],["MCP3208","12","8","SPI",""],["ADS1115","16","4","I²C","mit PGA, differentiell"],["ADS1015","12","4","I²C","schneller"]],"mono":[],"fett":true},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["DAC","Bits","Schnittstelle"],"zeilen":[["MCP4725","12","I²C"],["MCP4921","12","SPI"],["PCM5102","32 (Audio)","I²S"]],"mono":[],"fett":true,"titel":"DAC-Bausteine"},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"merke","text":"**Abtasttheorem (Nyquist):** Abtastrate f_s > 2 · f_max des Signals. Sonst entstehen **Aliasing**-Fehler (falsche Frequenzen). Bei Audio: 44,1 kHz für 20 kHz."},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"pi","text":"Der Pi hat **keinen ADC**. Nimm MCP3008 (SPI) oder ADS1115 (I²C) oder lass einen Pico/Arduino die analogen Messwerte liefern."},{"t":"h2","text":"ADC-Auflösung"},{"t":"text","text":["Aus Bits und Referenzspannung: Auflösung in mV und Wandlerwert."]},{"t":"formel","name":"ADC-Auflösung","f":"LSB = UREF / 2^N","text":""},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"Beim Raspberry Pi Pico: 12 Bit, Referenz 3,3 V → 0,8 mV pro Stufe."},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"ESP32-ADC ist nicht linear – kalibrieren."},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"Arduino Uno: 10 Bit, 5 V → 4,9 mV pro Stufe."}],"siehe":["passiv:ntc","schnittstellen:spi"],"symbol":"voltmeter","gruppe":""},{"id":"takt","titel":"Takt, Baudrate & Zeit","kurz":"Teiler, Timer, Baudraten-Fehler","tags":["takt","baudrate","uart","timer","teiler","frequenz","prescaler"],"bloecke":[{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Baudrate","Bit-Dauer","Bytes/s (8N1)"],"zeilen":[["9600","104,2 µs","960"],["19200","52,1 µs","1 920"],["38400","26,0 µs","3 840"],["57600","17,4 µs","5 760"],["115200","8,68 µs","11 520"],["230400","4,34 µs","23 040"],["921600","1,085 µs","92 160"],["1 000 000","1 µs","100 000"]],"mono":[],"fett":true,"titel":"UART (8 Datenbits, kein Paritätsbit, 1 Stopbit = 10 Bits pro Byte)"},{"t":"rechner","titel":"UART-Übertragungszeit","felder":[["b","Baudrate","","115200"],["n","Bytes","","1000"]],"ergebnis":[["t","Dauer (10 Bits/Byte)","n*10/b","s"],["bps","Nutzdaten","b*8/10","Bit/s"]]},{"t":"rechner","titel":"Baudratenfehler (AVR)","felder":[["f","CPU-Takt","Hz","16M"],["b","Baudrate","","115200"]],"ergebnis":[["ubrr","UBRR (gerundet)","round(f/(16*b)-1)","","zahl"],["real","Tatsächliche Baudrate","f/(16*(round(f/(16*b)-1)+1))","","zahl"],["err","Fehler","(f/(16*(round(f/(16*b)-1)+1))-b)/b","","proz"]]},{"t":"formel","name":"Timer-Überlauf","f":"T = (2ⁿ · Vorteiler) / f_CPU","text":"Für 16 Bit, 16 MHz, Vorteiler 1024: 4,19 s."},{"t":"rechner","titel":"Timer","felder":[["f","CPU-Takt","Hz","16M"],["n","Zählerbits","","16"],["p","Vorteiler","","1024"]],"ergebnis":[["t","Überlaufzeit","2**n*p/f","s"],["fo","Überlauf-Frequenz","f/(2**n*p)","Hz"]]},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Fehler UART","Bewertung"],"zeilen":[["< 2 %","in Ordnung"],["2–3 %","grenzwertig"],["> 3 %","Übertragungsfehler wahrscheinlich"]],"mono":[],"fett":true},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"Probleme mit Zeichenmüll (zufällige Zeichen) auf der seriellen Schnittstelle: **Baudrate falsch**, Pegel falsch (5 V ↔ 3,3 V) oder TX/RX nicht gekreuzt."}],"siehe":["passiv:quarz","schnittstellen:uart","digital:wissen_flanke","schnittstellen:busse"],"symbol":"quarz","gruppe":""},{"id":"wissen_pi-strom","titel":"GPIO-Strombelastung","kurz":"Wie viel Strom darf ein Pin liefern?","tags":["gpio","strom","belastung","pin","mikrocontroller","limit","mA","led"],"bloecke":[{"t":"text","text":["Mikrocontroller-Pins sind keine Leistungsausgänge. Immer die Stromgrenze beachten."]},{"t":"bauteil","e":{"id":"pi-strom","name":"GPIO-Strombelastung","titel":"Wie viel Strom darf ein Pin liefern?","kurz":"Mikrocontroller-Pins sind keine Leistungsausgänge. Immer die Stromgrenze beachten.","familie":"Grundlagen","gehaeuse":"","pins":[],"spannung":"","hinweise":["Raspberry Pi: ca. 16 mA pro GPIO, ca. 50 mA insgesamt (empfohlen). Pico: bis ca. 12 mA pro Pin (konfigurierbar). Arduino Uno: 20 mA empfohlen (40 mA absolut max).","Größere Lasten über Transistor / MOSFET schalten (siehe „MOSFET-Schalter“).","LED mit Vorwiderstand: bei 3,3 V und 5 mA reichen oft 330 Ω.","Niemals einen Pin direkt an +U oder GND kurzschließen."],"tags":"gpio strom belastung pin mikrocontroller limit mA led","kat":"wissen","uid":"wissen:pi-strom"}}],"siehe":["bt_wissen:wissen_pi-strom"],"gruppe":""}]}